diff --git a/libhegel/RELEASE.md b/libhegel/RELEASE.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..2901cf90
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libhegel/RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+RELEASE_TYPE: patch
+
+This patch adds the draws a frontend needs to put libhegel behind an existing property-based testing API, prompted by an experiment running Hypothesis on libhegel:
+
+- `hegel_generate_integer_weighted(min_value, max_value, shrink_towards, keys, weights, len)`: one plain integer choice whose fresh draws take `keys[i]` with probability `weights[i]` and otherwise the ordinary distribution, and which shrinks toward `shrink_towards` rather than 0. Replay and shrinking never consult the weights.
+- `hegel_generate_integer_forced(min_value, max_value, forced)`: records a caller-chosen value as a forced integer choice, as `hegel_generate_boolean` already can for booleans, so a frontend whose own code decides a value at a choice position keeps its sequence aligned with the engine's.
+- `hegel_string_generator_text_ranges(min_size, max_size, ranges, ranges_len)`: a text generator over an alphabet given as explicit sorted, disjoint codepoint ranges, exactly as the caller computed it. Surrogates are removed as for `hegel_string_generator_text`.
+- `hegel_test_case_choices(tc, out)`: the choices a live test case has recorded so far, as the same base64 blob a failure's reproduction uses, for a frontend that generates whole values natively and learns the sequence after the fact.
+- `allow_nan` is now accepted alongside finite float bounds: NaN comes with the usual NaN probability and in-range values otherwise, where the combination used to be an invalid argument.
+
+It also builds the "diffuse" pool of a wide integer draw (up to 256 bignum powers of two) only when that category is selected, as the "interesting" pool already was; an integer draw over a range wider than `i128`, such as `integers()` clamped to `2**128`, goes from about 160 microseconds to about 3, with the same values from the same seed.
